sequenceDiagram
    participant App as Your App (flow state machine)
    participant GT as Game Thread (engine)
    participant RT as Render Thread (engine)
    participant AT as Audio Thread

    Note over App,AT: IN-GAME PAUSE — two clocks, one frozen.<br/>A main menu is a LIVE World birds fly, clouds waft, nothing paused.<br/>paused and scale persist across swaps. only flow code changes them.
    App->>GT: ctx.set_paused(true)
    Note over GT: FIXED phase runs 0 ticks (accumulator frozen)<br/>physics + fixed gameplay halt · world renders frozen-but-alive
    GT->>App: update(ctx) keeps running — dt = 0, real_dt live
    App->>GT: pause-menu UI entities animate on real_dt
    App->>AT: duck gameplay bus, keep UI bus (game decision, via mixer)
    App->>GT: ctx.set_paused(false) — simulation resumes, no time debt

    Note over App,AT: WORLD SWAP — MainMenu → Loading → Game (flow enum lives in the App)
    App->>GT: ctx.audio.play(menu_music) — voice lives in the mixer, not the World
    App->>GT: ctx.begin_world_load(game_world_descriptor)
    GT->>GT: build successor World in the background:<br/>spawn from documents · stream cells · warm assets (normal async paths)
    loop while loading — the CURRENT World keeps rendering (it IS the loading screen)
        App->>GT: ctx.world_load_progress(handle)
        GT->>App: asset/cell readiness → progress bar
    end
    opt fade-to-black (pure game composition)
        App->>GT: full-screen UI quad, alpha up on real_dt
    end
    App->>GT: ctx.swap_world(handle, CaptureLastFrame)
    Note over GT: applied at end of frame — old World tears down properly:<br/>behavior shutdowns · deferred despawns · emitters stop ·<br/>physics world rebuilds from new descriptions (OQ 20)
    GT->>RT: EXTRACT — scene-reset delta + the new World's first spawns
    RT->>RT: retained RenderScene clears wholesale, repopulates
    GT->>App: transition texture handle (old world's last presented frame)
    App->>GT: crossfade: UI fades the captured frame out over the live new World
    Note over App,AT: menu music is still playing — commands-audio outlives worlds. the App crossfades it via ctx.audio once gameplay begins
